      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 7 November 2026</p>
      <p>This policy explains the cookies used by FRIEND CHAT. Cookies are small files or values stored by your browser to keep the service working.</p>

      <h2>Cookies used by the service</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Session cookie:</strong> keeps your signed-in session working. The current session-cookie setting expires after up to seven days. It is an essential cookie and is not used for advertising.</li>
        <li><strong>Remember-me cookie:</strong> if you choose “Remember me” when signing in, a cookie named <code>userToken</code> is set to keep you signed in. It is configured to expire after 30 days. You can avoid it by leaving “Remember me” unselected.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These cookies support authentication and account security. If you block or delete them, sign-in or other account features may not work as expected.</p>

      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>The current application code does not load an analytics or Google AdSense script. It does contain Google AdSense publisher-account metadata, which by itself does not set advertising cookies. If advertising or analytics is added, this policy will be updated and any consent required by applicable law will be requested before non-essential cookies are used.</p>

      <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
      <p>You can manage or delete cookies in your browser settings. Browser controls differ, and deleting essential cookies may sign you out.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>For questions about this policy, contact the service operators, Dominik Szczerbal and Wojciech Majchrzak, in Poland at ul. Śmigielska 34, 64-030 Śmigiel, or email <a href="mailto:support@friendchat.space">support@friendchat.space</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
